# Commands a fresh sandbox should be able to recall before anything has been run.
# start_timestamp is 2026-07-26T00:00:00Z, one second apart, in the order below.
# Why a fixed date and not 0: `hist` turns the column into a datetime, and 0 made
# every seeded row read as 1970. Why fixed and not `date now` at import: the
# importer dedups on start_timestamp, so a moving stamp would re-insert the whole
# seed on every `cozy sandbox-state history seed`.
[[command_line, cwd, start_timestamp, duration_ms, exit_status];
 ["claude --dangerously-skip-permissions", "/home/agent/workspace", 1785024000000, 0, 0],
 ["claude --dangerously-skip-permissions --resume", "/home/agent/workspace", 1785024001000, 0, 0],
 ["cozy sync-repos", "/home/agent/workspace", 1785024002000, 0, 0],
 ["cozy sandbox-state history export", "/home/agent/workspace", 1785024003000, 0, 0],
 ["cozy sandbox-state history import", "/home/agent/workspace", 1785024004000, 0, 0],
 ["claude-nu messages", "/home/agent/workspace", 1785024005000, 0, 0],
 ["claude-nu messages --include-responses", "/home/agent/workspace", 1785024006000, 0, 0],
 ["claude-nu sessions --all-projects | claude-nu messages", "/home/agent/workspace", 1785024007000, 0, 0],
 ["claude-nu sessions", "/home/agent/workspace", 1785024008000, 0, 0],
 ["claude-nu export-session --to sessions", "/home/agent/workspace", 1785024009000, 0, 0],
 ["cozy docs claude", "/home/agent/workspace", 1785024010000, 0, 0],
 ["cozy docs nushell", "/home/agent/workspace", 1785024011000, 0, 0],
 ["zellij attach -c sandbox", "/home/agent/workspace", 1785024012000, 0, 0]]
